From: Fathom <fathom@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: gadget: bring the core back on a reset after a session end

When the cable comes out, dwc2 sees the session end, reports the disconnect
and leaves lx_state at L3. On the next connection the host's USB reset only
re-initialises the core if we were connected, which after a session end we
never are; ENUMDONE then queues the setup request, ep_queue refuses it
(-EAGAIN: lx_state != L0), and every control transfer fails. On the HiFi
Walker H2 (Ingenic X1000, device-only VBUS sensing through the Type-C chip),
a Mac retried for 15 s and more after each replug, until something else
re-initialised the core (an OTG role change, or rebinding the gadget).

Treat a reset received at L3, with a gadget driver bound, as the new
connection it is.

Signed-off-by: Fathom
---
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/gadget.c
@@ -3778,6 +3778,8 @@
 	if (gintsts & (GINTSTS_USBRST | GINTSTS_RESETDET)) {
 		u32 usb_status = dwc2_readl(hsotg, GOTGCTL);
 		u32 connected = hsotg->connected;
+		/* The cable came out (session end): the core was left off (L3) */
+		bool was_off = hsotg->lx_state == DWC2_L3 && hsotg->driver;
 
 		dev_dbg(hsotg->dev, "%s: USBRst\n", __func__);
 		dev_dbg(hsotg->dev, "GNPTXSTS=%08x\n",
@@ -3791,7 +3793,12 @@
 		/* Reset device address to zero */
 		dwc2_clear_bit(hsotg, DCFG, DCFG_DEVADDR_MASK);
 
-		if (usb_status & GOTGCTL_BSESVLD && connected)
+		/*
+		 * A host resetting us after a session end is a new connection:
+		 * bring the core back, or every request fails with -EAGAIN
+		 * (lx_state != L0) and the host retries in vain.
+		 */
+		if ((usb_status & GOTGCTL_BSESVLD && connected) || was_off)
 			dwc2_hsotg_core_init_disconnected(hsotg, true);
 	}
 
